# Accepted vulnerability findings for the Trivy scans (checked by tools/trivy_scan.py).
# Only after checking that the finding cannot be exploited in this program. Every entry needs:
#   - an expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD, at most 6 months ahead) – after that the finding blocks again,
#   - a reason in the comment line directly above it (what, why not exploitable, who/when).
# Example:
#   # libfoo in the base image: only used by apt at build time, not reachable at runtime – checked 2026-10-25
#   CVE-2099-12345 exp:2027-04-25
# apt/libapt-pkg 3.0.3 in the base image: apt is only used while building the image (package installation), the
# running program never calls it and pip/apt are not reachable from the web app. Fix apt 3.0.4 is not yet in the
# Debian archive state the build uses – the weekly security update takes it. Checked 2026-11-05.
CVE-2026-109518 exp:2026-11-19
